.he "dcheck (1)                 8/16/26                   dcheck (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
dcheck
- check the link count of every file
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
dcheck [ -v ] [ -i inumber ... ] filesystem
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Dcheck makes two passes over the directories of the named file system.
The first counts how many directory entries name each inode; the
second compares that count against the link count stored in the inode
itself.  An inode whose link count differs from the number of
references to it is printed, with both numbers.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
OPTIONS
.in +5
.br
.in +10
.ti -10
-v	Be verbose.

.ti -10
-i inumber	Print the name of the given inode, in the form
inumber directory/name, as it is found in the first pass.

.in -10
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
This is the v6 dcheck: it validates link counts, which is what the
name comes from, and does nothing else.  It does not look at the free
list or the blocks; icheck (1) does that.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
icheck (1), ncheck (1)
